From dfbfa251d893357d441b02aa0cf7493df2c6a955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 11:00:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06890/11362] [outer-loop] ARC bp35 round-6: honest null, L6
 route mapped to a lethal notch exit

Round-6 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on bp35 reconfirmed the L5 prefix on
three fresh environments, then disambiguated L6's glyphs (the narrow
dark-red glyph is the player, cyan blocks are one-use gravity switches)
and mapped a route: solidify the lower X blocks, align over the shelf,
flip the first cyan switch, cross into the hazard-free right shaft, then
flip the second cyan switch to reverse gravity into a protected notch --
but exiting that notch is lethal in every direction tested (left blocked,
right kills). That exit is the concrete remaining blocker.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
